# VoltTracker environment variables — reference copy.
#
# Nothing in this repo auto-loads a .env file: the Gradle build, the Playwright
# dashboard suite and the CI workflows all read these straight from the process
# environment. So this file is documentation of the variables that actually get
# consumed, not a config file the build parses. Copy it to `.env` (gitignored)
# and `source` it, or just export the handful you need.
#
# Every value below is a placeholder. Real credentials belong in GitHub Actions
# secrets or in mobile/android/keystore.properties, both of which stay out of
# git — see the release signing section at the bottom.

# --- Android SDK -----------------------------------------------------------
# Used by mobile/android/build.gradle to locate `adb` for the device-status and
# `localDoctor` tasks. ANDROID_HOME is checked first, ANDROID_SDK_ROOT is the
# fallback; if neither is set the build falls back to `adb` on PATH.
ANDROID_HOME=/Users/you/Library/Android/sdk
#ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=/Users/you/Library/Android/sdk

# --- Toolchain escape hatch ------------------------------------------------
# The build pins Node to the major version in .node-version (currently 24) and
# fails fast on anything else. Set this to 1/true/yes to downgrade that failure
# to a warning. Temporary local use only — CI never sets it, so a build that
# only works with the override set is a build that is about to break.
# See mobile/android/docs/dependencies.md.
#VOLTTRACKER_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED_NODE=0

# --- Dashboard E2E (mobile/android/dashboard-e2e) --------------------------
# Port for the static server that serves the built dashboard to Playwright.
# Both static-server.cjs and playwright.config.js default to 8099.
#DASHBOARD_E2E_PORT=8099

# Absolute path to a browser binary for Playwright to drive instead of its own
# managed download. Useful when the sandboxed browser download is unavailable.
#PW_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome

# Output directory for the opt-in screenshot spec. before-screens.spec.js skips
# itself entirely unless this is set.
#SHOT_DIR=./build/screenshots

# Set by GitHub Actions. Locally it only changes Playwright behaviour (forbids
# test.only, enables one retry, switches the reporter), so leave it unset.
#CI=

# --- Release signing (CI only) ---------------------------------------------
# These are GitHub Actions secrets, consumed by the "Decode release keystore
# from secrets" step in .github/workflows/release.yml, which reconstitutes
# mobile/android/keystore.properties + app/release.keystore for
# signingConfigs.release. Do NOT put real values in a .env file. For local
# release builds, write mobile/android/keystore.properties directly (gitignored)
# instead of exporting these.
#
#ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64=<base64 of your release.keystore>
#ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=<keystore password>
#ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS=<key alias>
#ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD=<key password>
